<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAFRICA MARCH SPENDING UP 12.2 PCT AT 17.5BLN RAND.</title>
<headline>SAFRICA MARCH SPENDING UP 12.2 PCT AT 17.5BLN RAND.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total exchequer issues in</p>
<p>the first month of the 1997/98 (April) financial year were</p>
<p>17.512 billion rand, which is 12.2 percent higher than the same</p>
<p>period last year, the Finance Department said.</p>
<p>Total revenue for the same period rose 4.7 percent to 10.952</p>
<p>billion rand:</p>
<p>(rand bln)		Apr '97  Apr '96  </p>
<p>Exchequer issues	17.512   15.602   </p>
<p>Total revenue	   10.952   10.456   </p>
<p>Borrowing requirement  5.362    3.979   </p>
<p>Total financing	  4.452    8.228   </p>
<p>Main sources of revenue:</p>
<p>			   Mch '97   Mch '96  Apr/Mch '97  Apr/Mch '96</p>
<p>    Income tax	   9.209    6.329    82.873	 68.652</p>
<p>    Sales tax/VAT	3.758    2.388    35.902	 32.316</p>
<p>    Customs and Excise 1.675    1.599    19.725	 17.683</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
